      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GRIFTER (7) should strip much fitter second-up after resuming over 1200m here and finishing fourth as the favourite after struggling in the heavy ground. He has more to offer and with the blinkers on for the first time, he can make amends. Follow your money. BIG VEE (1) was excellent first-up here off a long spell, going down by only a head over this distance. He should take improvement from that run and should go close to winning this. FLAWS AND SINS (3) strips fitter second up, and did have market support on debut. Stick with him. TIKIELA (6) ran on well enough to finish fourth third up from a spell at Hamilton last week over 1100m, and she figure in the top 3 this time, especially with a senior hoop on here. ",
